===Etymology===
Recorded since 1577, probably a {{rebracketing|en|[[an]] [[otch]]|nocap=1}}, from {{der|en|frm|oche||notch}}, itself from the {{der|en|fro|-}} verb {{m|fro|ochier||to notch}}, of uncertain origin, but possibly related to {{cog|fr|hocher}} and {{cog|en|nick||small cut, notch}}.

