# {{lb|en|informal}} A [[level]] or [[degree]].
#: {{ux|en|This car is a '''notch''' better than the other.}}
#: {{ux|en|Can you speak a '''notch''' louder, please?}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|date=20 June 2014|author=Daniel Taylor|title=World Cup 2014: Uruguay sink England as Suárez makes his mark|url=http://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jun/19/england-uruguay-match-report-group-d
|passage=a better team might also have done more to expose Uruguay’s occasionally brittle defence, but England’s speed of thought and movement in their attacking positions was a good '''notch''' or two down from the Italy game.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261013065111/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jun/19/england-uruguay-match-report-group-d|archivedate=13 October 2026}}
#* {{quote-video game|en|developer=w:BioWare|title={{w|Mass Effect: Andromeda}}|location=Redwood City|publisher=Electronic Arts|year=2017|system=PC|scene=Ugh!|oclc=1261299044|text=Your doctor is one of the nosiest asari I've ever met. And that's saying A LOT. She needs to take it down four or five '''notches''', or I won't be long for this show.}}
# {{lb|en|electronics}} A portion of a [[mobile phone]] that overlaps the edge of the [[screen]], used to house a [[camera]], [[sensor]]s etc. while maximizing screen space.

