===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[cut]] a notch in (something).
#: {{syn|en|indent}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To record (a [[score]] or similar) by making notches on something.
#: {{ux|en|The tribe's hunters '''notch''' their kills by notches on each's axe's handle.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[join]] by means of notches.
# {{lb|en|transitive|informal}} To [[achieve]] (something); to add to one's score or record of successes.
#: {{synonyms|en|notch up}}
#: {{ux|en|The team '''notched''' a pair of shutout wins on Sunday.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} {{syn of|en|nock|id=fit|t=to fit (an arrow) to a bow}}.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1885|author=John Niles Hubbard|title=An Account of Sa-go-ye-wat-ha, Or Red Jacket, and His People, 1750-1830|page=31|passage='''Notching''' an arrow on the string of his tried and unerring bow, he raised his sinewy arms {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To change in small graduations.
#: {{ux|en|to '''notch''' back a salary}}

